# Push After Every Task

- After completing and verifying a task that changed repository files, commit and push only the changes belonging to that task.
- Preserve unrelated or pre-existing working-tree changes; never include them just to make the tree clean.
- If pushing is blocked by authentication, conflicts, or remote rejection, report the exact blocker instead of claiming completion.
- For read-only tasks or tasks that do not change repository files, do not create an empty commit.
